t to get as close to your customers  as possible so people are having  problems you want to be able to answer  those questions really quickly respond  quickly be able to make fixes you know  as quick as you can the  one thing that differentiates a small  start-up from a big company is  flexibility and speed so you want to  take advantage of that you want to wait  a long time to get back to people if  you're finding people asking similar  questions or having problems with  something you want to make a change  right away and try to keep that customer  as long as you can make them happy and  if you can overturn a bad situation to a  positive you're more likely to keep that  customer for a long term and also  they're going to tell their friends but  the great experience I had nobody goes  and tells a friends about the great  experience it had used in a customer  service software online right it's from  the personal touch they get from dealing  with people at the company so especially  when you're in start-up mode I would not  use a software company I would try to do  it personally get the feedback from the  customers build closer relationships and  be able to take the feedback to give you  to make your product better as you grow  I then would look at delegating that so  having somebody on the team and on my  team I don't so we have six thousand  people who write for my website I am NOT  managing those relationships I used to  and then I took just took up way too  much of my time so I brought on somebody  and that's her main functions to work  with our authors and answer their  questions and build new innovations to  help them out and so you want to have  somebody who is responsive in an ideal  world kind of give your options you can  look at even a place like odesk calm to  try to find people to help on the  support site at hopefully are maybe a  cheaper rate then you would get locally  if budget is a really big issue for you  if you absolutely have to have to have  to 